{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-424", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/424", "wordCount": 2036, "segments": [{"start": 16.0, "text": "Good morning."}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "I'm Alex Brown, an Engineer in"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "Core ML."}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "And today, we are going to"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "present Create ML for Object"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "Detection."}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "In the What's New in Machine"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "Learning session, you were"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "introduced to the new Create ML"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "It provides a really"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "approachable way to build custom"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "machine learning models to add"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "to your applications."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "In this session, we're going to"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "dig a little deeper into two"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "specific templates."}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "Object detection, which works"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "with images, and sound"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "classification."}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "Let's get started with object"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "detection."}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "Object detection enables your"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "application to identify"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "real-world objects captured by"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "your device's camera, and"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "respond based on their presence,"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "position, and relationship."}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "You can download object"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "detectors from the web which"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "know the difference between"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "broad categories of objects."}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "But by training a custom machine"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "learning model on your own data,"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "you can teach your application"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "about the subtle differences"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "between individual animals, hand"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "gestures, street signs, or game"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "tokens."}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "If you've used machine learning"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "with Apple before, you may"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "already be familiar with image"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "classification."}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "With image classification, you"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "build a model which can provide"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "a single simple description of"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "an image."}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "This image we might describe as"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "outdoors or park, or for a"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "particular application, dog."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "But what if we're interested in"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "more than one object in the"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "scene?"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "In this case, object detection"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "can come to the rescue."}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "It can identify multiple objects"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "within your photograph, and"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "provide the location, size, and"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "label for each one."}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "This can enable your application"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "to do more sophisticated things"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "using your camera, but in order"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "to do that, we need to go into"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "more detail when teaching the"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "model about your images."}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "To train an object detector, you"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "need to annotate each image with"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "labeled regions that you would"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "like the model to recognize."}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "The bounding box for your"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "annotated objects starting at"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "the center of each object of"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "interest and having a size,"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "height, and width, this is"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "measured in pixels from the top"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "left-hand corner of your image"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "to the center of each object of"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "interest."}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "You bundle together all of these"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "annotations, label, position,"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "and size, in a JSON file in the"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "following format."}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "You can download tools from the"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "web to help you build these, but"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "make sure they use the same"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "coordinate system the Create ML"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "app expects."}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "Once you've assembled your"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "annotations, simply drop them"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "into the same folder as the"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "images they describe, and that's"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "it."}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "Your training data is ready."}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "So now we know how to create"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "training data for object"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "detection."}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "Let's consider a real case."}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "My colleague, Scott, has got a"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "great idea for building a math"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "game that is really engaging for"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "kids, and uses real-world dice"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "to provide the questions."}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "You can hear more about this"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "application in session 228,"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "Creating Great Apps Using Core"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "ML and AR Kit."}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "So, Scott asked me to help build"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "a model for his game, and I"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "suggested using Apple's Create"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "ML application to train an"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "object detector."}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "Scott has already sent me the"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "training data."}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "He took a bunch of images of"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "dice from different angles and"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "with different values on the"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "top, and he's annotated them,"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "drawing bounding boxes around"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "the top face and adding a label,"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "counting the number of pips on"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "each dice."}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "So, now we've got our data"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "ready. Let's take a look at how we can"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "use the Create ML application to"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "build our model."}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "So first of all, let's just"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "check the data."}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "You can see we've put all of our"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "images in a folder, and each one"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "contains multiple dice, and"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "we've gathered together the"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "annotations in a single JSON"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "file."}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "So now, I'll open the Create ML"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "I can do this from inside X"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "code's menu, or I can just use"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "Spotlight."}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "When the Create ML application"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "opens, it gives us the option to"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "access documents we already"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "created."}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "Here, we want a new project."}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "First, you'll see the template"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "picker, which give you a"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "collection of machine learning"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "model types to select from."}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "In this case, we want an image"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "object detector."}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "I give it a name, so we can"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "identify it later on, and fill"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "in a few details."}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "Here, you can see the main"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "window with the training view on"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "the right-hand side. It has already selected the"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "input tab, ready for our"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "training data."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "I can drag that straight into"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "the training data well."}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "Even before training the model,"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "the application takes a look at"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "the data, and checks it's in the"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "right format, contains images"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "rather than sound, for instance,"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "and has a JSON file, which"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "correctly describes them."}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "It also provides some initial"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "statistics."}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "Here, we can see we have around"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "1,000 images, and there are six"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "classes, six, for the six sides"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "of a six-sided dice."}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "That's perfect."}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "We can do some other things on"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "this screen."}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "For instance, we can supply"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "testing data, to allow us to"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "compare the performance of two"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "different models."}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "Also, we can set some advanced"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "parameters, tuning the way the"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "model trains."}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "But we don't need to worry about"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "any of that right now, we're"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "actually ready to train."}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "Let's hit the play button, and"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "see what happens."}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "Training has begun."}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "It takes us instantly to the"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "Training tab, where we can see"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "the progress of the model"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "training."}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "This is a graph of loss."}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "Loss decreases as the model gets"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "better and better."}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "So we should see this converge"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "down to the bottom of the graph."}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "Object detection takes a lot"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "longer to train than image"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "classification."}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "I estimate this is probably"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "going to take an hour or more."}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "We don't want to wait for that,"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "so I've already trained a model"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "using this data."}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "Here we are, and I can jump to"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "the same training tab that we"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "just looked at."}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "You can see that the loss has"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "neatly declined, showing the"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "performance of the model has"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "really increased over the time"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "it took to train."}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "There's a couple of other things"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "that you should really have a"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "look at on this screen."}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "First of all, the overall"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "performance."}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "Ninety-two percent, which is a"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "really great number for an"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "object detector."}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "We also want to have a look and"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "check that we have consistent"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "performance across all of the"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "classes."}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "The classes, 1 to 6, each here"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "has 90% or more, and they're"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "about the same value."}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "This is important because it"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "shows that it is performing"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "equally well on the six sides of"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "the dice."}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "For a game of dice, where"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "fairness is important, that's"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "pretty important."}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "So, the model has told us"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "mathematically that it's pretty"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "good, but how do we get"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "confidence that it's going to"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "work for our cases?"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "Well, we can use the output tab."}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "Scott sent me a test image to"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "try out before I send the model"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "back to him, so let's drag that"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "in now."}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "That's looking pretty great."}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "You can see that it is"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "identified, the five dice in the"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "scene."}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "It has correctly drawn the box"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "around their top faces, and by"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "clicking through, 6, 1, 5, we"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "can see each label, and the"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "confidence is assigned."}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "That's performing really well."}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "So, if I was building my own"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "app, I could go ahead and drag"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "the model that has been produced"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "and use it within Xcode."}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "I think Scott is probably"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "waiting for this model to build"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "his application."}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "But before we go there, there's"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "something I want to try."}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "While I was preparing for this"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "demo, playing with dice, and a"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "camera, and my computer, my son,"}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "who is 9, came over and asked"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "what I was doing."}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "Once I'd explained it, he got"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "pretty excited, and already"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "started coming up with an idea"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "for a game which had animals,"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "bears, and bats, and they"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "cooperate to collect bolts to"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "build a space ship."}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "And they use dice, colored dice,"}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "to level up for each different"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "kind of monster."}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "So we got his dice, and I"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "decided to try them with Scott's"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "model."}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "So the dice he's using are a"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "little bit different."}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "They're role-playing dice,"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "so let's see how the model"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "performs."}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "Using the Max Continuity Camera"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "feature, I can import an image"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "directly from my phone."}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "This is really great because it"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "means it's using the same glass,"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "the same camera that your"}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "application will use."}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "I take the photo and click Use"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "Photo."}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "And it's instantly analyzed it."}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "So let's take a moment to have a"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "look at what is going on here."}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "It has correctly spotted the two"}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "six-sided dice with pips, and it"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "has given them the right labels."}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "It has ignored most of the other"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "dice in the picture, except for"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "a couple over here."}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "It has given those the wrong"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "numbers."}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "So why is this?"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "The problem here is a difference"}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "in expectation."}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "Scott knows the dice that are"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "going to be used are six-sided"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "white dice with pips."}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "My son's idea of dice is quite"}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "different."}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "They're colored. They don't just have six sides."}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "So how might we address this in"}, {"start": 709.0, "text": "our application?"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "Well, either we can insist on"}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "using the dice that maybe are"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "supplied with the game in the"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "classroom, or we can train the"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "model with these dice."}, {"start": 720.0, "text": "There are two ways we can"}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "approach this."}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "Either we can decide that only"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "the six-sided dice with pips are"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "valid, but we want to exclude"}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "the other dice, in which case,"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "we just need to take photographs"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "containing both kinds of dice,"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "and just label the six-sided"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "ones."}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "Or if we were building a bear"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "and bat game, we might like to"}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "add the other kinds of dice into"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "our model, and label those too,"}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "either just using their numbers"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "or adding extra labels to"}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "distinguish the colors."}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "Red 6, black 4, etc."}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "So let's send this model on to"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "Scott, so he can build his demo."}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "I can use the Share button to"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "simply mail the model."}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "And there we have it."}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "So, we've seen how you can"}, {"start": 788.0, "text": "use the Create ML application to"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "train your object detector on"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "training data that you've"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "collected."}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "There are some things I'd like"}, {"start": 796.0, "text": "you to consider when building"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "that training data."}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "Firstly, you should have a"}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "balanced number of images with"}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "annotations for each class."}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "This tells the algorithm that"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "you consider each of these to be"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "equally important, and we can"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "build a model which performs"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "equally well on all of the"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "classes."}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "Secondly, you are going to need"}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "a bunch of images."}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "I recommend you start with 30"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "images with annotations for each"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "class you want the model to"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "recognize, and increase that"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "number if you find performance"}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "isn't good enough, or if your"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "subjects are particularly"}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "complicated."}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "For instance, they look"}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "different on different sides."}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "What about the issue we"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "encountered with the different"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "colored dice?"}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "Well, that's not the only way"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "pictures might differ."}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "We recommend you consider how"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "the application will be used in"}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "the real world."}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "Your users may not have studio"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "lighting, standard dice, and a"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "beautiful wooden desk to work"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "with."}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "Perhaps ask your friends to"}, {"start": 860.0, "text": "collect additional data in"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "different scenarios, such as"}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "indoor lighting, outdoors in the"}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "sun, different backgrounds, and"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "add in different objects that"}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "you aren't using for your model."}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "This helps the model generalize"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "really well."}, {"start": 879.0, "text": "Something that may be surprising"}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "to you, if you've used an image"}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "classifier before, is that one"}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "label is enough."}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "This is because by explaining a"}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "part of your image that is a"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "dog, you're also saying that the"}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "rest of it isn't, and the model"}, {"start": 893.0, "text": "trains accordingly."}, {"start": 895.0, "text": "So, for example, if you were"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "building an application to count"}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "the number of pickle jars in"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "your fridge, you don't need to"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "label all of the other"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "condiments. It automatically infers that"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "they're not pickle jars."}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "Once you've built your model,"}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "and you want to add the"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "functionality into your"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "application, we recommend you"}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "use the vision framework."}, {"start": 920.0, "text": "The vision framework can"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "seamlessly integrate live camera"}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "as well as video into your model"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "flow."}, {"start": 929.0, "text": "And that's all there is to"}]}
